              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "This sample Power BI report accompanies the blog post \"Visualising Data with Extreme Outliers in Power BI: A Practical Guide\", available at endjin.com/blog."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "It demonstrates a number of approaches for visualising data containing extreme outliers. The sample data set, shown in the table below, contains information on 120 items that move through a series of workflow states from \"Received\" to \"Complete\". Each row details the time the item spent in a single workflow state."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " Items are considered \"outliers\" if their total processing time in all states is more than 120 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The report showcases a number of visualisation techniques, with the calculated columns and measures necessary to generate them."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
